  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ramprakash vs State Of M.P. on 8 March, 2025 Author: Anand Pathak Bench: Anand Pathak 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Gwalior Lok Adalat Hon'Ble Shri Justice Anand Pathak & Shri Harish Dixit, Senior Advocate On The 8th Of March, 2025 Criminal Revision No.44 of 2014 Ramprakash Vs. State Of Madhya Pradesh ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Appearance: Shri Pawan Vijaywargiya - Advocate for the petitioner. Shri R.S. Yadav - Public Prosecutor for the respondent/State. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Order",
    "facts": "It is the submission of learned counsel for the petitioner that the present case pertains to offence under Section 7(1) read with 16(1)(ka) (1) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act. The offence is of the year 1999 and petitioner suffered more than 7 days' incarceration as pre and post trial confinement. Further from the date of incident, petitioner suffered almost 27 years' ordeal of trial. Hence, it is submitted that the case of petitioner be considered for the sentence which is already Ramprakash vs State Of M.P. on 8 March, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/34972416/ 1 undergone by him, for which he is ready to pay compensation/fine at higher side in view of provisions of Section 357 of Cr.P.C. 3. Learned counsel for the respondent/State opposed the prayer.",
    "arguments": "However, he fairly accepted that if petitioner is ready to pay the enhanced fine amount/compensation, then only his case for undergone may be considered so that enhanced amount (fine) can be given to the complainant.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "However, he fairly accepted that if petitioner is ready to pay the enhanced fine amount/compensation, then only his case for undergone may be considered so that enhanced amount (fine) can be given to the complainant.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
